From 847f374cbfe9ae1f1afede95a732424b2d081580 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:23:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FixedPointSolver: review of the iterative solvers of the
 factory

- Sequential prediction without kernels: diagonal set to one at the
  essential degrees of freedom (the sequential bilinear forms of MFEM keep
  the diagonal of the stiffness), as in parallel and with the kernels. An
  iterative solver preconditioned by the elastic operator now solves the
  prediction in one iteration (GMRES: 2 21 fixed point iterations before,
  2 2 now).
- Options of the iterative solvers and DiscardLinearSolverFailure read
  before being applied: a refused call leaves the solver unchanged.
- getFactoryArgument: the error message names the parameter and the
  expected forms.
- Documentation: warnings of the iterative solvers printed if their
  VerbosityLevel is given; FGMRES and variable preconditioners; lower
  bound of the regularization of Anderson's method.
- Tests: NewtonK0 with the prediction by the elastic operator, the linear
  solver of the elastic operator (a counting solver) being replaced
  between two time steps (the destroyed solver is not called again),
  NewtonK0 predictions made by the conjugate gradient, NewtonK0 with the
  default iterative solver of the tangent operator, prediction by GMRES,
  refusals checked on their error messages, Newton references computed
  with the prediction and the number of time steps of each case. The
  mutations of these fixes are detected.
